  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Between vs And on 21 July, 2020 Author: M.Ganga Rao Bench: M.Ganga Rao [ 2696 ] In The High Court Of Andhra Pradesh At Amaravati wf Tuesday, The Twenty First Day Of July, 4\" Two Thousand And Twenty :Present: The Honourable Sri Justice M.Ganga Rao Criminal Petition No: 2544 Of 2020 Between: 4. Nunna Venkata Buchi Raju @ Raju, S/o Veerabadrarao, Age.55 years, R/o Cooperative Bank, Tallarevu Village and Mandal, East Godavari District. 2. Satti Ramgopal Reddy, S/o Somi Reddy, Age. 34 years, R/o Balaji Reddy Vari Veedhi, Ravulapalem Village and Mandal, East Godavari District. 3. Kamadi Venkanna Babu, S/o Naga Raju, Age. 34 years, 4** Street, Old age Home, Yaanam, Pandicheri State 4. Bommaraju Krishna, S/o Ramachandar, Hindu, Age. 33 years, R/o Behind Sarada Theatre, Kodandaram Nagar, Street No.1, Saroornagar, Hyderabad _..Petitioner/Accused 2 to 5 And",
    "facts": "The case of the prosecution is that on 19.06.2020 at about 03.30 PM the police noticed the petitioners loading contraband from Mahindra Truck Auto: into an Auto. On that the SI of police apprehended the petitioners and on interrogation of the petitioners in the presence of mediators, it is revealed that the petitioners used to purchase Gutkha, Khainees, Cigarettes and Ganja from A1, who is resident of Hyderabad. Petitioner no.4 brought the contraband from A1 ina Mahindra Truck and while the petitioners were shifting the 'contraband from Mahindra Truck into Auto, the police apprehended the petitioners. The SI arrested the petitioners in the presence of mediators under a mediators report and seized prohibited Gutkha, Khaini packets and cigarette packets from the possession of the petitioners. 5 % kgs of ganja is also seized from the petitioners under cover of mediators report.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that insofar as the offences under COTP Act are concerned, this Court in a series of judgments Oakhwn> held that police have no jurisdiction to register the crime and investigate and if any offence is made out, the Food Safety Officer is alone entitled to investigate the crime in terms of Section 42 of Food Safety and Standards Act. Learned counsel further submitted that the petitioners are falsely implicated in the case and the alleged seizure of the contraband of 5 % Kgs Ganja is made contrary to the provision of Section 50 of NDPS Act and that merits of the case apart, the quantity of Ganja involved is 5 % Kgs and it is not a commercial quantity and the bar under Section 37 of NDPS Act does not apply to the case on hand and the petitioners are in judicial custody since 19.06.2020.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that insofar as the offences under COTP Act are concerned, this Court in a series of judgments Oakhwn> held that police have no jurisdiction to register the crime and investigate and if any offence is made out, the Food Safety Officer is alone entitled to investigate the crime in terms of Section 42 of Food Safety and Standards Act. Learned counsel further submitted that the petitioners are falsely implicated in the case and the alleged seizure of the contraband of 5 % Kgs Ganja is made contrary to the provision of Section 50 of NDPS Act and that merits of the case apart, the quantity of Ganja involved is 5 % Kgs and it is not a commercial quantity and the bar under Section 37 of NDPS Act does not apply to the case on hand and the petitioners are in judicial custody since 19.06.2020.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
